{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Moshe journeyed.</b> He moved them against their will — for the Egyptians had adorned their horses with ornaments of gold and silver and precious stones, and Israel was finding them in the sea. And the plunder of the sea was greater than the plunder of Egypt, as it says: ״תּוֹרֵי זָהָב נַעֲשֶׂה לָּךְ עִם נְקֻדּוֹת הַכָּסֶף״ (Song of Songs 1). Therefore he needed to move them against their will."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:33.181952730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}